    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0520" n="396" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3607</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Group to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 3.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to our letter of November
                        28th<anchor n="89" xml:id="d360-f1"/> with respect to the proposed extension
                    of the Pacific Development Corporation loan to China, we beg to state that the
                    Chinese Government paid the interest <pb facs="0521" n="397" xml:id="pg397"/>
                    due the Corporation on December 1st, and the lending banks in the American Group
                    have approved the extension of the Corporation’s note held by them for six
                    months on the terms outlined in the two letters of November 25th and November
                    28th from the Corporation to the Group, copies of which are attached.<anchor
                        n="90" xml:id="d360-f2"/></p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. P. Morgan</hi> &amp; Co.<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">For the American Group</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
